["create","MIGH",1783050391,"5207ee28-cdd8-48e6-98dc-7da179d4a40d",{"title":"Migration-path hardening: retire residual defect sources in runRepoSetup legacy migration","type":"story","scope":["cmd/armature/bootstrap.go","internal/adapters/git.go","cmd/armature/bootstrap_test.go","internal/adapters/git_internal_test.go","cmd/armature/bootstrap_migration_matrix_test.go (new)"],"acceptance":["make check green","arm validate exits 0","TestMigrationInvariantMatrix_P1 passes for all cases"],"definition_of_done":"All residual defect sources in the legacy-migration path are fixed (lossy ops-log copying, HEAD~1 rollback, locale-sensitive git parsing, user-hook interference, silent stranded backups) and a failure-injection permutation test enforces the no-silent-data-loss invariant. make check green with coverage/mutation not regressed from 86.3%/100%.","priority":"high","confidence":"draft"}]
["create","MIGH-T1",1783050391,"5207ee28-cdd8-48e6-98dc-7da179d4a40d",{"title":"Locale-stable git output parsing (force C locale in cmdContext)","parent":"MIGH","type":"task","scope":["internal/adapters/git.go","internal/adapters/git_internal_test.go"],"acceptance":["TestCmdContextForcesCLocale passes","go test ./internal/adapters/ -count=1 green"],"definition_of_done":"Every *exec.Cmd built by adapters.Client carries LC_ALL=C and LANG=C, so string matching on git output (e.g. CommitPaths' \"nothing to commit\") is stable under any user locale. No signature changes. Whole adapters package passes.","priority":"high","confidence":"draft"}]
["create","MIGH-T2",1783050391,"5207ee28-cdd8-48e6-98dc-7da179d4a40d",{"title":"Internal migration commits bypass user git hooks (--no-verify)","parent":"MIGH","type":"task","scope":["internal/adapters/git.go","cmd/armature/bootstrap.go","cmd/armature/bootstrap_test.go"],"acceptance":["TestRunRepoSetupMigrationSurvivesHostileUserHooks_P1 passes","TestRunRepoSetupCommitFailureRollsBackUncommittedMigration_P1 passes","go test ./cmd/armature/ -count=1 green"],"definition_of_done":"New CommitPathsNoVerify on adapters.Client (same contract as CommitPaths plus --no-verify); orphan init commit in CreateOrphanBranch uses --no-verify; the three migration/bootstrap commit call sites in bootstrap.go switched to CommitPathsNoVerify. A hostile user pre-commit hook can no longer abort migration. Existing test TestRunRepoSetupMigrationCommitFailureNamesBackupDir_P1 rewritten per plan to TestRunRepoSetupCommitFailureRollsBackUncommittedMigration_P1 using a bogus-GPG failure trigger.","priority":"high","confidence":"draft"}]
["link","MIGH-T2",1783050391,"5207ee28-cdd8-48e6-98dc-7da179d4a40d",{"dep":"MIGH-T1","rel":"blocked_by"}]
["create","MIGH-T3",1783050391,"5207ee28-cdd8-48e6-98dc-7da179d4a40d",{"title":"SHA-based migration rollback (replace HEAD~1 reset)","parent":"MIGH","type":"task","scope":["cmd/armature/bootstrap.go","cmd/armature/bootstrap_test.go"],"acceptance":["TestRollbackLegacyMigrationResetsToPreMigrationSHA_P1 passes","go test ./cmd/armature/ -run 'TestRollbackLegacyMigration|TestRunRepoSetup' -count=1 green"],"definition_of_done":"migrateLegacySingleBranchOps returns (migrated bool, backupDir string, preMigrationSHA string, err error) with preMigrationSHA non-empty iff HEAD actually moved; rollbackLegacyMigration(repoPath, backupDir, preMigrationSHA) resets hard to the recorded SHA when non-empty, else renames the backup back. runRepoSetup passes the SHA through both rollback call sites and its two 'backup left at' guards check preMigrationSHA != \"\". All existing rollback tests pass.","priority":"high","confidence":"draft"}]
["link","MIGH-T3",1783050391,"5207ee28-cdd8-48e6-98dc-7da179d4a40d",{"dep":"MIGH-T2","rel":"blocked_by"}]
["create","MIGH-T4",1783050391,"5207ee28-cdd8-48e6-98dc-7da179d4a40d",{"title":"Merge divergent ops logs on migration instead of skipping","parent":"MIGH","type":"task","scope":["cmd/armature/bootstrap.go","cmd/armature/bootstrap_test.go"],"acceptance":["TestMigrationMergesDivergentOpsLogs_P1 passes","TestMergeAppendOnlyLogIdenticalIsNoOp_P2 passes","go test ./cmd/armature/ -run 'TestMigration|TestCopyLegacy|TestCopyRecursive|TestRunRepoSetupMigration' -count=1 green"],"definition_of_done":"New helper mergeAppendOnlyLog(srcPath, dstPath) (appended int, err error) appends each non-empty legacy line not already present (exact byte match) to the destination, preserving order. copyLegacyOpsToNewWorktree routes ops/*.log files with an existing destination through the merge instead of skip-on-exists; non-.log files keep skip semantics. Identical logs are a no-op.","priority":"high","confidence":"draft"}]
["link","MIGH-T4",1783050391,"5207ee28-cdd8-48e6-98dc-7da179d4a40d",{"dep":"MIGH-T3","rel":"blocked_by"}]
["create","MIGH-T5",1783050391,"5207ee28-cdd8-48e6-98dc-7da179d4a40d",{"title":"Surface stranded migration backups on every bootstrap run","parent":"MIGH","type":"task","scope":["cmd/armature/bootstrap.go","cmd/armature/bootstrap_test.go"],"acceptance":["TestRunRepoSetupReportsStrandedBackups_P2 passes","go test ./cmd/armature/ -run TestRunRepoSetup -count=1 green"],"definition_of_done":"New helper listMigrationBackups(repoPath) []string returns sorted base names of .armature.migrated-* dirs (best-effort, nil on read errors). runRepoSetup prints an informational Note listing existing backups after the migration attempt — never an error, never auto-deleted.","priority":"medium","confidence":"draft"}]
