["create","NXTTN-S5",1783480525,"5207ee28-cdd8-48e6-98dc-7da179d4a40d",{"title":"The CLI Grammar Contract","parent":"NXTTN","type":"story","definition_of_done":"docs/design/cli-grammar-contract.md's plan is fully executed: the 46-command audit and rename map exist, TTY detection is consolidated, renames land with no compatibility aliases, and the grammar conformance test enforces the rules going forward.","priority":"medium","confidence":"draft"}]
["create","NXTTN-S5-T1",1783480525,"5207ee28-cdd8-48e6-98dc-7da179d4a40d",{"title":"46-command audit table against deep-module boundaries and flag conventions; produce the rename map","parent":"NXTTN-S5","type":"task","scope":["docs/design/cli-command-audit.md (new)"],"acceptance":["docs/design/cli-command-audit.md enumerates every surviving command","every command has a stated deep-module correspondence or an explicit 'stays flat' ruling with reason","the rename map has no alias or sunset-date fields"],"definition_of_done":"docs/design/cli-command-audit.md has one row per surviving command (post-NXTTN-S2 cuts) citing its deep-module correspondence (or lack thereof per ADR 0011's signal rule) and its flag-convention compliance (positional-vs---issue rule, --format coverage); a rename map lists old-name to new-name pairs for every command needing a change, with no alias/sunset fields since renames break immediately.","priority":"medium","confidence":"draft"}]
