["create","LNGHZN-S2",1783521994,"5207ee28-cdd8-48e6-98dc-7da179d4a40d",{"title":"Scope-disjoint wave planning (arm ready --waves)","parent":"LNGHZN","type":"story","scope":["cmd/armature/ready.go","internal/ready/compute.go","internal/ready/waves.go (new)","docs/adr/0012-scope-disjoint-wave-planning.md (new)","docs/commands.md","internal/skillsembed/skills/armature-coordinator/references/parallel-dispatch.md"],"acceptance":["All sub-task acceptance criteria pass","make check green"],"definition_of_done":"arm ready gains a --waves mode that partitions the ready queue into scope-disjoint dispatch waves via greedy first-fit (priority tier as a hard boundary; conflict-degree ordering within a tier; ancestor/descendant exclusion; no wave-size cap), emitted as a new grouped array-of-waves shape for --format json/agent, additive to the unchanged plain arm ready output. An ADR codifies the scope-disjoint-is-not-contract-safe non-goal and the other resolved design decisions from the F2 grilling session (docs/design/next-work-sequencing.md). No new op type; --waves is a pure computed view.","priority":"high","confidence":"draft"}]
