["create","LNGHZN-S2-T1",1783521994,"5207ee28-cdd8-48e6-98dc-7da179d4a40d",{"title":"arm ready --waves: partition engine, flag, and grouped output","parent":"LNGHZN-S2","type":"task","scope":["cmd/armature/ready.go","internal/ready/compute.go","internal/ready/waves.go (new)","internal/ready/waves_test.go (new)","docs/commands.md"],"acceptance":["TestComputeWaves_PartitionsScopeDisjointEntries_REQ_LNGHZN_S2_T1 passes","TestComputeWaves_RespectsPriorityTierBoundary_REQ_LNGHZN_S2_T1 passes","TestComputeWaves_OrdersByConflictDegreeWithinTier_REQ_LNGHZN_S2_T1 passes","TestComputeWaves_ExcludesAncestorDescendantPairs_REQ_LNGHZN_S2_T1 passes","TestReadyCommand_WavesFlagGroupedOutput_REQ_LNGHZN_S2_T1 passes","make check green"],"definition_of_done":"arm ready --waves partitions ComputeReady's ready-eligible entries into scope-disjoint dispatch waves using greedy first-fit: priority tier is a hard boundary (a critical item is never delayed behind a lower-priority item or vice versa to improve packing); within a tier, items are ordered by scope-conflict degree (most-constrained first) rather than the existing depth/blocks/ID tie-break; ancestor/descendant pairs (via dag.Graph's descendant queries) are excluded from conflict comparison; overlap is computed via claimPkg.ScopesOverlap (internal/claim/overlap.go). Output for --format json/agent is a new top-level {\"waves\": [[entry,...],...]} grouped shape scoped to the --waves flag; plain arm ready (no --waves) is unchanged. No wave-size cap. No new op type or persisted state.","priority":"high","confidence":"draft"}]
["link","LNGHZN-S2-T1",1783521994,"5207ee28-cdd8-48e6-98dc-7da179d4a40d",{"dep":"TOPTIER-S17-T1","rel":"blocked_by"}]
["create","LNGHZN-S2-T2",1783521994,"5207ee28-cdd8-48e6-98dc-7da179d4a40d",{"title":"ADR: codify the wave-planning non-goal and resolved design decisions","parent":"LNGHZN-S2","type":"task","scope":["docs/adr/0012-scope-disjoint-wave-planning.md (new)"],"acceptance":["docs/adr/0012-scope-disjoint-wave-planning.md exists with Status: Accepted","ADR cross-references docs/design/next-work-sequencing.md's F2 grilling session decisions","make check green"],"definition_of_done":"docs/adr/0012-scope-disjoint-wave-planning.md states explicitly that arm ready --waves guarantees freedom from file-level scope conflict only, never from shared-contract/interface drift (citing the 2026-07-06 cross-task-format-drift finding as evidence), and records: the already-shipped companion-check correction, the advisory/pre-dispatch-only relationship to the coordinator's wave-manifest (WAVE_TASK_IDS/WAVE_BASE_SHA remain coordinator-skill-recorded, not engine-sourced), and the stateless/no-new-op-type guarantee.","priority":"medium","confidence":"draft"}]
["create","LNGHZN-S2-T3",1783521994,"5207ee28-cdd8-48e6-98dc-7da179d4a40d",{"title":"Update armature-coordinator skill guidance for arm ready --waves","parent":"LNGHZN-S2","type":"task","scope":["internal/skillsembed/skills/armature-coordinator/references/parallel-dispatch.md"],"acceptance":["make validate-skills passes","make check green"],"definition_of_done":"internal/skillsembed/skills/armature-coordinator/references/parallel-dispatch.md documents arm ready --waves as the engine-computed alternative to manually reasoning about scope-disjoint parallel dispatch, while explicitly retaining today's prose-recorded WAVE_TASK_IDS/WAVE_BASE_SHA manifest step unchanged (per the ADR's advisory-only clarification) and noting the contract-safety non-goal from the ADR.","priority":"medium","confidence":"draft"}]
