["create","LNGHZN-S5",1784485922,"5207ee28-cdd8-48e6-98dc-7da179d4a40d",{"title":"Managed worktree lifecycle (LH F1)","parent":"LNGHZN","type":"story","acceptance":["All child tasks merged","arm validate passes with no errors"],"definition_of_done":"Worktrees are a first-class managed resource: the claim op records the worktree path, arm worktree list reconciles worktrees against claim state, arm worktree gc removes worktrees for merged/cancelled issues, and project-type mitigations (go.work exclusion) are applied at provision time.","priority":"high","confidence":"draft"}]
["create","LNGHZN-S5-T1",1784485922,"5207ee28-cdd8-48e6-98dc-7da179d4a40d",{"title":"Record the worktree path in the claim op","parent":"LNGHZN-S5","type":"task","scope":["internal/claim/claim.go","internal/ops/ops_worktree_test.go (new)","cmd/armature/claim.go"],"acceptance":["TestClaimOpRecordsWorktreePath_REQ_LNGHZN_S5_T1 passes","TestLegacyClaimOpWithoutWorktreePathReplays_REQ_LNGHZN_S5_T1 passes","make check green"],"definition_of_done":"arm claim --worktree records the created/updated worktree's absolute path as a field on the claim op; materialization exposes it on the issue state so recovery tooling can find the worktree deterministically. Legacy claim ops without the field still replay cleanly.","context_files":["docs/schemas/plan.schema.json"],"priority":"high","confidence":"draft"}]
["create","LNGHZN-S5-T2",1784485922,"5207ee28-cdd8-48e6-98dc-7da179d4a40d",{"title":"arm worktree list|gc: reconcile worktrees against claim state","parent":"LNGHZN-S5","type":"task","scope":["cmd/armature/worktree.go (new)","cmd/armature/worktree_test.go (new)","internal/worktree/reconcile.go (new)","internal/worktree/reconcile_test.go (new)"],"acceptance":["TestWorktreeListFlagsOrphans_REQ_LNGHZN_S5_T2 passes","TestWorktreeGCRemovesMergedWorktrees_REQ_LNGHZN_S5_T2 passes","make check green"],"definition_of_done":"arm worktree list shows each managed worktree with its bound issue and claim status, flagging orphans (worktree with no live claim) and ghosts (claim recording a missing worktree). arm worktree gc removes worktrees whose issues reached merged/cancelled; a --dry-run flag previews removals. No state is mutated except worktree removal.","priority":"high","confidence":"draft"}]
