["create","LNGHZN-S7",1784485922,"5207ee28-cdd8-48e6-98dc-7da179d4a40d",{"title":"Make configuration honest — wire or delete every dead knob (LH D1)","parent":"LNGHZN","type":"story","acceptance":["All child tasks merged","arm validate passes with no errors"],"definition_of_done":"Every field in .armature/config.json either governs the behavior its name implies or is deleted: default_ttl drives arm claim's TTL default, token_budget is read by render-context, low_stakes_push_threshold is wired or removed. Unknown fields are rejected at decode; doctor verifies config health; docs drop the inert-knob footnotes.","priority":"high","confidence":"draft"}]
["create","LNGHZN-S7-T1",1784485922,"5207ee28-cdd8-48e6-98dc-7da179d4a40d",{"title":"Wire default_ttl, token_budget, and low_stakes_push_threshold (or delete)","parent":"LNGHZN-S7","type":"task","scope":["internal/config/config.go","internal/config/config_test.go","cmd/armature/render_context.go"],"acceptance":["TestDefaultTTLGovernsClaim_REQ_LNGHZN_S7_T1 passes","TestTokenBudgetHonoredByRenderContext_REQ_LNGHZN_S7_T1 passes","make check green"],"definition_of_done":"default_ttl is the single source of arm claim's --ttl default; token_budget is honored by standalone render-context assembly; low_stakes_push_threshold is either wired as an actual auto-push trigger or deleted with a config-migration note — the decision recorded in the task outcome. No config field's documented behavior carries a caveat afterward.","priority":"high","confidence":"draft"}]
