["transition","TOPTIER-S4",1784602671,"5207ee28-cdd8-48e6-98dc-7da179d4a40d",{"to":"done","outcome":"Delivered recovery-state-machine.md (21-cell status x claim-liveness matrix), arm doctor --fix (releases expired claims, reconciles missing-worktree claims; fleet-wide done-without-commit repair deliberately deferred as unsafe to automate — documented, reviewed yellow), and arm ready's distinct expired-claims section (text + JSON, backward-compatible). All 3 tasks merged, reviewed (2 green, 1 yellow with documented rationale). Story-scoped arm validate --strict clean; repo-wide warnings/STALE sources are pre-existing backlog from unrelated stories, not introduced by this work. Along the way, fixed a pre-existing arm doctor D3 false-positive (deleted note-only ops incorrectly flagged as orphaned) that was blocking all coordination work, on its own branch/commit."}]
["amend","LNGHZN-S3-T1",1784680461,"5207ee28-cdd8-48e6-98dc-7da179d4a40d",{"scope":["cmd/armature/harness_hook.go","cmd/armature/heartbeat.go","internal/claim/claim.go","internal/claim/claim_test.go","internal/ops/types.go","cmd/armature/harness_hook_test.go (new)"],"acceptance":["TestHookEmitsRateLimitedHeartbeat_REQ_LNGHZN_S3_T1 passes","TestHookSkipsHeartbeatWhenUnbound_REQ_LNGHZN_S3_T1 passes","TestShouldHeartbeatSkipsAlreadyStaleClaim_REQ_LNGHZN_S3_T1 passes","TestHookHeartbeatSourceIsAutoHook_REQ_LNGHZN_S3_T1 passes","TestManualHeartbeatSourceIsManual_REQ_LNGHZN_S3_T1 passes","TestHookHeartbeatFiresOnBlockedToolCall_REQ_LNGHZN_S3_T1 passes","internal/harnesshook.Evaluate signature and Decision struct unchanged by this task","make check green"],"definition_of_done":"Hook emits at-most-once-per-~5min heartbeats (debounce from last emission, fixed constant, independent of TTL) on every PreToolUse for bound+unstale claims, before allow/block. Rate-limit state: disposable per-worker+issue file in OS temp dir. Op reuses OpHeartbeat + new Source field (auto-hook/manual). All I/O (cache, claim materialization, op-append via existing appendLowStakesOp) stays in cmd/armature/harness_hook.go; decision logic is a pure internal/claim.ShouldHeartbeat wrapping IsClaimStale. Append failures: swallowed for the tool call, warned to stderr, no retry. Always-on, no config flag. See decisions on this issue for full rationale."}]
["amend","LNGHZN-S3-T2",1784680467,"5207ee28-cdd8-48e6-98dc-7da179d4a40d",{"acceptance":["docs/harness-hook.md has an autonomic-heartbeats section consistent with the shipped behavior, including the Source field and TTL-vs-interval doctor warning","internal/skillsembed/skills/armature-worker/SKILL.md keeps manual arm heartbeat guidance only for long non-tool thinking stretches","make check green (skill lint/golden transcripts pass)"],"definition_of_done":"docs/harness-hook.md gains an autonomic-heartbeats section: fixed ~5min debounce interval, always-on with no config flag, disposable per-worker+issue temp-dir cache, Source field (auto-hook vs manual) on heartbeat ops, and the doctor warning when default_ttl is too low relative to the fixed interval (~3x margin). Worker skill drops guidance to manually heartbeat during active tool use, keeping manual arm heartbeat only for long non-tool thinking stretches."}]
["decision","LNGHZN-S3-T1",1784680484,"5207ee28-cdd8-48e6-98dc-7da179d4a40d",{"topic":"rate-limit cadence","choice":"debounce from last heartbeat emission (reset clock each time), fixed ~5min constant independent of configured TTL","rationale":"Simpler than wall-clock bucketing; composes directly with claim.IsClaimStale's lastActivity semantics","affects":["internal/claim/claim.go"]}]
["decision","LNGHZN-S3-T1",1784680484,"5207ee28-cdd8-48e6-98dc-7da179d4a40d",{"topic":"rate-limit state storage","choice":"disposable cache file, one per worker+issue pair, in OS temp dir","rationale":"Hook runs as a fresh process per tool call (no daemon, I1); cache avoids an ops-log read on every PreToolUse. Not source of truth -- losing it only causes redundant heartbeats, never incorrectness. OS temp dir keeps it out of the worktree/git and isolates concurrent worktrees without a shared-writer race","affects":["cmd/armature/harness_hook.go"]}]
["decision","LNGHZN-S3-T1",1784680484,"5207ee28-cdd8-48e6-98dc-7da179d4a40d",{"topic":"append failure handling","choice":"swallow for the tool-call decision (never block), but write a warning to hook stderr; no retry","rationale":"Fully silent failure would recreate the exact invisible-staleness problem this proposal exists to fix, one layer down","affects":["cmd/armature/harness_hook.go"]}]
["decision","LNGHZN-S3-T1",1784680484,"5207ee28-cdd8-48e6-98dc-7da179d4a40d",{"topic":"heartbeat op provenance","choice":"reuse ops.OpHeartbeat, add a Source field (auto-hook vs manual)","rationale":"IsClaimStale only needs the latest timestamp regardless of source, but provenance is needed for forensic/debugging value the proposal itself leans on (was the worker actually driving tool calls, or was a stale claim papered over manually)","affects":["internal/ops/types.go","cmd/armature/heartbeat.go"]}]
["decision","LNGHZN-S3-T1",1784680484,"5207ee28-cdd8-48e6-98dc-7da179d4a40d",{"topic":"stale-claim race","choice":"hook must check the claim is not already stale (internal/claim.ShouldHeartbeat wrapping IsClaimStale) before emitting; single implementation, not duplicated in the hook","rationale":"Without this check the hook could resurrect a claim already reassigned after going stale, reintroducing the double-claim conflict class this proposal is meant to prevent","affects":["internal/claim/claim.go"]}]
["decision","LNGHZN-S3-T1",1784680484,"5207ee28-cdd8-48e6-98dc-7da179d4a40d",{"topic":"interval vs configured TTL","choice":"fixed constant in code (not TTL-derived); doctor/config-validation instead warns if default_ttl is too low relative to the constant","rationale":"Honors the DoD wording (constant in code), keeps the hot path free of a config read, but still catches a TTL configured so short the heartbeat can't keep up","affects":["internal/config/config.go"]}]
["decision","LNGHZN-S3-T1",1784680484,"5207ee28-cdd8-48e6-98dc-7da179d4a40d",{"topic":"rollout","choice":"always-on, no config flag/opt-out","rationale":"Correctness fix, not an optional feature; an off-by-default heartbeat reproduces the D1 'config that lies' problem for the exact class of bug this proposal targets","affects":["cmd/armature/harness_hook.go"]}]
["decision","LNGHZN-S3-T1",1784680484,"5207ee28-cdd8-48e6-98dc-7da179d4a40d",{"topic":"block/allow interaction","choice":"heartbeat fires unconditionally on every PreToolUse, before the allow/block decision, including on blocked calls","rationale":"Heartbeat is a liveness signal, not a reward for compliant behavior; gating it on DecisionAllow would induce false staleness for workers stuck hitting scope walls -- the opposite of this proposal's goal","affects":["cmd/armature/harness_hook.go"]}]
["decision","LNGHZN-S3-T1",1784680485,"5207ee28-cdd8-48e6-98dc-7da179d4a40d",{"topic":"hexagonal architecture boundary","choice":"all I/O (cache file, claim materialization, op-append via appendLowStakesOp) stays in cmd/armature/harness_hook.go; heartbeat decisioning is a separate pure function in internal/claim, not folded into internal/harnesshook.Evaluate/Decision","rationale":"Project rule: imperative/I/O code must live in cmd/, not internal/. appendLowStakesOp already lives in cmd/armature (package main) and harness_hook.go is already in that package, so no extraction into internal/ is needed. Heartbeating is orthogonal to the allow/block policy Decision already encodes, so it stays a separate call, independently testable","affects":["internal/harnesshook/evaluator.go","internal/claim/claim.go","cmd/armature/harness_hook.go"]}]
["amend","LNGHZN-S3-T1",1784680497,"5207ee28-cdd8-48e6-98dc-7da179d4a40d",{"definition_of_done":"Hook emits at-most-once-per-~5min heartbeats (debounce, fixed constant, TTL-independent) on every PreToolUse for bound+unstale claims, before allow/block. Rate-limit state: disposable per-worker+issue file in OS temp dir. Op reuses OpHeartbeat + new Source field. All I/O stays in cmd/armature/harness_hook.go; decisioning is pure internal/claim.ShouldHeartbeat. Failures: swallowed+warned, no block. Always-on. See recorded decisions for rationale."}]
["link","LNGHZN-S4-T1",1784680520,"5207ee28-cdd8-48e6-98dc-7da179d4a40d",{"dep":"TOPTIER-S5","rel":"blocked_by"}]
["amend","LNGHZN-S4-T1",1784680527,"5207ee28-cdd8-48e6-98dc-7da179d4a40d",{"scope":["internal/deliverygate/gate.go (new)","internal/deliverygate/gate_test.go (new)","internal/claim/overlap.go","internal/claim/overlap_test.go"],"acceptance":["TestDeliveryGateCleanTree_REQ_LNGHZN_S4_T1 passes","TestDeliveryGateScopeContainment_REQ_LNGHZN_S4_T1 passes","TestDeliveryGateCommitReference_REQ_LNGHZN_S4_T1 passes","TestClaimIsWithinScope_REQ_LNGHZN_S4_T1 passes","make check green"],"definition_of_done":"A new internal/deliverygate package evaluates a worktree against an issue via three checks: (1) clean tree — git status --porcelain is empty (subsumes untracked-build-artifact detection; .armature/ is gitignored, needs no special-casing), (2) scope containment — delivery diff vs base is a subset of declared scope using a new internal/claim.IsWithinScope primitive (reuses existing glob internals in overlap.go, no separate matcher in deliverygate), (3) commit reference — at least one commit matches the repo's conventional-commit scope format for the issue ID per docs/conventions.md, not a bare substring search. Returns a structured result listing each failed check with a remediation string; performs no state mutation.","context_files":["internal/claim/overlap.go","docs/conventions.md"]}]
["amend","LNGHZN-S4-T2",1784680535,"5207ee28-cdd8-48e6-98dc-7da179d4a40d",{"acceptance":["TestTransitionDoneBlockedByGate_REQ_LNGHZN_S4_T2 passes","TestTransitionDoneGateOverride_REQ_LNGHZN_S4_T2 passes","TestTransitionDoneNoBoundWorktreeFailsClosed_REQ_LNGHZN_S4_T2 passes","make check green"],"definition_of_done":"arm transition --to done runs the delivery gate in the bound worktree before appending the op and refuses with per-check remediations on failure; ships enforcing immediately on merge, no warn-only/staged-rollout mode. If no bound worktree can be found or inspected, the gate fails closed (refuses the transition with a remediation to re-bind or pass --skip-delivery-gate), never fails open. An explicit override flag --skip-delivery-gate exists, unrestricted at the CLI layer (no human-vs-agent detection attempted; enforced socially via the worker skill), and its use is always recorded in the transition op's note. Transitions to other states are unaffected."}]
["note","LNGHZN-S4-T1",1784680540,"5207ee28-cdd8-48e6-98dc-7da179d4a40d",{"msg":"Grilling-session decision: .armature/ is now gitignored repo-wide (PR #85, landed out of band). The clean-tree check needs no .armature/ special-casing — plain git status --porcelain already excludes it.","note_id":"note-1784680540598421413"}]
["note","LNGHZN-S4-T2",1784680540,"5207ee28-cdd8-48e6-98dc-7da179d4a40d",{"msg":"Grilling-session decision: --skip-delivery-gate is intentionally unrestricted at the CLI layer — there is no reliable way to distinguish human vs agent invocation, so enforcement is social (worker skill, T3) plus the audit trail (recorded in the transition op's note). Do not add a warn-only/staged-rollout mode; the gate ships enforcing from the moment it merges.","note_id":"note-1784680540715645724"}]
["amend","LNGHZN-S4-T1",1784680554,"5207ee28-cdd8-48e6-98dc-7da179d4a40d",{"definition_of_done":"A new internal/deliverygate package evaluates a worktree against an issue via three checks — clean tree, scope containment, commit reference — and returns a structured result with per-check remediations; performs no state mutation. See notes for check semantics."}]
["note","LNGHZN-S4-T1",1784680554,"5207ee28-cdd8-48e6-98dc-7da179d4a40d",{"msg":"Check semantics: (1) clean tree = git status --porcelain empty, subsumes untracked-build-artifact detection (no separate check), .armature/ needs no special-casing since it's gitignored. (2) scope containment = delivery diff vs base is subset of declared scope via new internal/claim.IsWithinScope, reusing overlap.go's private glob internals — no separate matcher in deliverygate. (3) commit reference = at least one commit matches the conventional-commit scope format (e.g. fix(ISSUE-ID): ...) per docs/conventions.md, not a bare substring search.","note_id":"note-1784680554965751462"}]
["amend","LNGHZN-S4-T2",1784680559,"5207ee28-cdd8-48e6-98dc-7da179d4a40d",{"definition_of_done":"arm transition --to done runs the delivery gate before appending the op, refusing with per-check remediations on failure, enforcing from the moment it merges. --skip-delivery-gate provides an explicit override, recorded in the transition op's note. Transitions to other states are unaffected. See notes for edge cases."}]
["note","LNGHZN-S4-T2",1784680559,"5207ee28-cdd8-48e6-98dc-7da179d4a40d",{"msg":"Edge cases: no bound worktree found at transition time -\u003e fail closed (refuse with remediation to re-bind or pass --skip-delivery-gate), never fail open/skip silently. --skip-delivery-gate is unrestricted at the CLI layer (no human-vs-agent detection); enforced socially via the worker skill (T3). No warn-only/staged-rollout mode — ships enforcing immediately.","note_id":"note-1784680559644655959"}]
["amend","NXTTN-S3",1784684835,"5207ee28-cdd8-48e6-98dc-7da179d4a40d",{"definition_of_done":"Tokens are a governed budget the way coverage already is: make context-report prices every static agent-facing artifact (skills, glossary, key docs) using a bytes/4 token estimate, per-artifact budgets grouped by class with a ratchet (budgets may only shrink, except via a dedicated budget-only commit) are enforced by a check wired into make check, and the coordinator skill is trimmed as the first application. Dynamic artifacts (render-context output, --format agent payloads) are explicitly out of scope for this story."}]
["amend","NXTTN-S3-T1",1784684840,"5207ee28-cdd8-48e6-98dc-7da179d4a40d",{"definition_of_done":"A context-report command/target enumerates static agent-facing artifacts — embedded skills, CONTEXT.md, docs/commands.md, concepts, use-cases — and reports byte and estimated token weight (bytes/4 heuristic, consistent with the existing token_budget config convention) per artifact, in human and JSON output. The token-estimation method is documented in the report output itself. Dynamic artifacts (render-context output, --format agent payloads) are out of scope for this task — noted as a known limitation, not silently dropped."}]
["amend","NXTTN-S3-T2",1784684842,"5207ee28-cdd8-48e6-98dc-7da179d4a40d",{"definition_of_done":"Per-artifact budgets (grouped by class — skills, glossary, command docs — for reporting and ratchet-direction purposes) are declared in a checked-in budgets file. Ratchet policy: an artifact's budget may only shrink, except via a dedicated commit that touches only the budgets file (a visible, reviewable increase, not silently bundled into a feature change — reviewer-enforced convention, not mechanically gated). make check fails when an artifact exceeds its budget. Initial budget values are seeded at-or-above each artifact's current measured size so the gate starts green. Current offenders documented with a trim plan in docs/context-budgets.md."}]
["amend","NXTTN-S3-T3",1784684844,"5207ee28-cdd8-48e6-98dc-7da179d4a40d",{"acceptance":["Coordinator skill within its declared per-artifact budget per make context-report","internal/skilltranscript coordinator golden-transcript tests still pass via make check"],"definition_of_done":"The coordinator skill (largest single artifact, ~32KB) is trimmed to fit its declared per-artifact budget without breaking the coordinator golden-transcript test (internal/skilltranscript, shipped by TOPTIER-S1-T2): redundant prose cut, reference material moved to the skill's existing references/ directory where the format allows."}]
