["amend","NXTTN-S3-T2",1784684858,"5207ee28-cdd8-48e6-98dc-7da179d4a40d",{"definition_of_done":"Per-artifact budgets (grouped by class for reporting) are declared in a checked-in budgets file. Ratchet: a budget may only shrink, except via a dedicated commit touching only the budgets file (reviewable, reviewer-enforced convention, not mechanically gated). make check fails when an artifact exceeds its budget. Initial values seeded at-or-above current measured size so the gate starts green. Offenders documented with a trim plan in docs/context-budgets.md."}]
["create","task-1784684900",1784684900,"5207ee28-cdd8-48e6-98dc-7da179d4a40d",{"title":"Auto-provision worktree at default root with detached-checkout race fix","parent":"LNGHZN-S5","type":"task","scope":["cmd/armature/claim.go","cmd/armature/claim_test.go","cmd/armature/cmd_extra_test.go","cmd/armature/main_test.go","cmd/armature/merged_test.go"],"acceptance":["TestClaimAutoProvisionsWorktreeAtDefaultRoot_REQ_LNGHZN_S5_T4 passes","TestClaimDetachedCheckoutAvoidsBranchAlreadyCheckedOutRace_REQ_LNGHZN_S5_T4 passes","TestClaimWorktreeFlagIsBoolean_REQ_LNGHZN_S5_T4 passes","make check green"],"definition_of_done":"arm claim gains a boolean --worktree flag (replacing the removed --worktree \u003cpath\u003e form) that provisions a worktree at the hardcoded default root .worktrees/\u003cissue-id\u003e. Provisioning checks out the worktree detached at the base commit first, then creates/checks out the issue's branch inside the worktree, eliminating git's \"branch already checked out\" failure that the old create-branch-then-add-worktree order could hit. This is a breaking CLI change (alpha software, no back-compat obligation).","priority":"high"}]
["amend","LNGHZN-S6-T1",1784684905,"5207ee28-cdd8-48e6-98dc-7da179d4a40d",{"scope":["internal/errors/errors.go","internal/errors/errors_test.go","internal/output/agent_error.go","internal/output/agent_error_test.go","cmd/armature/main.go","cmd/armature/helpers.go","cmd/armature/helpers_test.go"],"acceptance":["TestStructuredErrorAgentEnvelope_REQ_LNGHZN_S6_T1 passes","TestStructuredErrorHumanRendering_REQ_LNGHZN_S6_T1 passes","TestStructuredErrorCodeRegistryPanicsOnDuplicate_REQ_LNGHZN_S6_T1 passes","TestMainDispatchBypassesClassifyErrorForStructuredErrors_REQ_LNGHZN_S6_T1 passes","make check green"],"definition_of_done":"internal/errors gains a concrete StructuredError type constructed via a domain-prefixed stable code (e.g. CLAIM-003, one const block per owning package), a one-line cause, an exitcodes.Code, and a next_actions list of fully-resolved shell command strings (using \u003cplaceholder\u003e only for values arm cannot supply). Codes are registered at construction time in a runtime registry that panics on duplicate registration. Human format renders \"Error [CODE]: cause\" followed by indented \"Try:\" lines per next_action. --format agent renders a nested JSON envelope {\"error\": {\"code\", \"cause\", \"next_actions\", \"exit_code\"}}, replacing the existing flat jsonErrorPayload for migrated commands. cmd/armature/main.go's dispatch is rewired: when the returned error is a StructuredError, it renders directly from the type's fields and skips classifyError's substring matching entirely; classifyError remains the fallback for errors that are not yet StructuredError. Errors without the type render unchanged."}]
["amend","LNGHZN-S6-T2",1784684910,"5207ee28-cdd8-48e6-98dc-7da179d4a40d",{"acceptance":["TestClaimErrorsCarryNextActions_REQ_LNGHZN_S6_T2 passes","TestReviewBundleErrorRemediation_REQ_LNGHZN_S6_T2 passes","TestTransitionErrorsCarryStructuredCode_REQ_LNGHZN_S6_T2 passes","make check green"],"definition_of_done":"The most agent-trafficked failure paths — claim (missing --worktree, scope conflict), transition (invalid target state, delivery-gate failures), review (bundle file errors, schema-invalid assessment), ready, and render-context — construct and return internal/errors.StructuredError values (per T1's contract) with a domain-prefixed code (e.g. CLAIM-003, TRANSITION-001), a one-line cause, the appropriate exitcodes.Code, and next_actions naming the exact, fully-resolved recovery command (placeholders only for values arm cannot supply, e.g. a new worktree path). Each migrated command's error codes are registered under that command's own const block, not a shared file."}]
["amend","LNGHZN-S6-T3",1784684917,"5207ee28-cdd8-48e6-98dc-7da179d4a40d",{"acceptance":["TestErrorCodeRegistryUnique_REQ_LNGHZN_S6_T3 passes","TestMigratedCommandsEmitValidAgentEnvelope_REQ_LNGHZN_S6_T3 passes","make check green"],"definition_of_done":"docs/error-contract.md specifies: the domain-prefixed code registry convention (one const block per owning package) and its stability guarantee (a code, once shipped, is never repurposed to a different meaning — may be retired, never reassigned, even pre-v0.1.0); the StructuredError type and its runtime registration/duplicate-panic mechanism; the human rendering format (\"Error [CODE]: cause\" + indented \"Try:\" lines); the agent JSON envelope shape ({\"error\": {\"code\", \"cause\", \"next_actions\", \"exit_code\"}}); and the rule that next_actions are fully-resolved commands with \u003cplaceholder\u003e syntax reserved for values arm cannot supply. A conformance test exercises registration across all migrated command packages to confirm no duplicate codes exist (via the runtime registry, not a static scan) and that each migrated command in T2's list emits a schema-valid envelope in --format agent."}]
