["amend","TOPTIER-S5-T1",1784685923,"5207ee28-cdd8-48e6-98dc-7da179d4a40d",{"acceptance":["TestHookConformance_REQ_TOPTIER_S5_T1 passes the full binding x tool x path matrix","matrix includes named rows for the out-of-scope-edit, stray-binary, and worktree-leak-into-main bypass cases, each asserted as deny","task is test-only: no changes to internal/harnesshook/evaluator.go or internal/harnesspolicy non-test files; any live bypass found by the matrix is flagged in the task outcome, not fixed in this task","make check green"],"definition_of_done":"A table-driven conformance suite covers every combination of binding state (bound active, bound inactive, unbound) x tool class x path (in scope, out of scope, outside worktree) with expected allow/deny/pass-through decisions, run in CI, and explicitly includes named table rows for the three dogfood bypass cases: out-of-scope Makefile edit (deny), stray binary left outside declared scope (deny), and worktree changes leaking into the main worktree (deny)."}]
["amend","TOPTIER-S5-T2",1784685929,"5207ee28-cdd8-48e6-98dc-7da179d4a40d",{"acceptance":["TestScopeViolationLogging_REQ_TOPTIER_S5_T2 passes (violations logged in pass-through)","TestDoctorScopeCheck_REQ_TOPTIER_S5_T2 passes for stray-binary and out-of-scope-file cases using ScopePolicy.CheckPaths, and for the main-worktree-leak case scoped to a task's declared scope","docs/harness-hook.md documents the violation log format"],"definition_of_done":"Out-of-scope operations are logged with a violation marker even when the hook passes through, and a doctor check flags out-of-scope artifacts after task completion by reusing ScopePolicy.CheckPaths: any untracked or modified path (including stray binaries) outside the task's declared scope glob, and uncommitted/untracked changes in the main worktree that correlate with an active or recently-completed task's declared scope. General main-worktree hygiene unrelated to a task's scope is out of scope for this check."}]
