["amend","NXTTN-S4-T1",1784686291,"5207ee28-cdd8-48e6-98dc-7da179d4a40d",{"scope":["docs/paved-road.md","cmd/armature/main.go","cmd/armature/paved_road_test.go"],"acceptance":["docs/paved-road.md is generated with zero unclassified leaf commands","TestPavedRoadHelpClassification_REQ_NXTTN_S4_T1 passes","make check green"],"definition_of_done":"Every cobra command carries paved-road/escape-hatch classification metadata (down to leaf subcommands). docs/paved-road.md is generated from that metadata: names the blessed pipeline step-by-step with the exact commands per step (behavioral steps like wave dispatch spell out the underlying commands, e.g. ready/claim/assign), includes the generated classification table with zero unclassified leaf commands, and includes the defaults audit (flags that exist only because the road was never chosen). Escape-hatch commands carry an explicit [escape hatch] marker in --help output, appended within the existing functional groups (Workflow/DAG/Sync/Admin) rather than a full re-grouping; paved-road commands are otherwise unchanged. A conformance test asserts the generated doc and the --help markers match the code-level classification metadata so they cannot drift. Defaults identified by the audit as safe to change (no test/skill/doc references the current default) are changed in this task; any default with existing dependents is left alone and recorded in the audit findings instead."}]
