["note","TOPTIER-S13",1784687052,"5207ee28-cdd8-48e6-98dc-7da179d4a40d",{"msg":"Design (grilled 2026-07-21), closes G3.1/G3.3 only (not G3.2's auto-dispatch option):\n\nScope: RecordWithDuplicateCheck in internal/review/record.go only (Record() unchanged).\n\nDisagreement = same DeliveryFingerprint, different overall Rating (not criterion-level/ResultFingerprint divergence). Exact duplicates (same ResultFingerprint) are excluded from comparison entirely.\n\nNew AssessmentAttestation fields (always populated, never overwrite existing Rating field):\n- EffectiveRating Rating — max(this.Rating, all qualifying same-fingerprint priors' Rating), using existing Green\u003cYellow\u003cRed ordering. Populated even with no priors (== own Rating).\n- IsDisagreement bool — true iff any qualifying prior has a different Rating than this attestation's own Rating.\n- ConflictsWithBundleID string, ConflictsWithRating Rating — set only when IsDisagreement is true; reference the highest-severity qualifying prior, ties broken by most recently appended.\n\nNo auto-dispatch of a tie-break reviewer (G3.2's second option) — out of scope, would touch coordinator/dispatch code beyond this story's Scope. A follow-up story can add escalation/dispatch on top of IsDisagreement.\n\nTest: TestReviewRecord_HandlesConflictingRatings_REQ_TOPTIER-S13 should cover: no-prior case (EffectiveRating==own Rating, IsDisagreement=false), agreeing priors (no disagreement), disagreeing prior (IsDisagreement=true, EffectiveRating=max, ConflictsWith* set to the more severe one), 3+ priors with mixed ratings (ConflictsWith* points at highest-severity, not just most recent), and exact-duplicate prior excluded from comparison.","note_id":"note-1784687052826513680"}]
["amend","TOPTIER-S13",1784687057,"5207ee28-cdd8-48e6-98dc-7da179d4a40d",{"definition_of_done":"arm review record defines and enforces reviewer-disagreement behavior for repeated assessments of the same delivery fingerprint: same DeliveryFingerprint + differing overall Rating sets IsDisagreement, EffectiveRating is the severity-max (Green\u003cYellow\u003cRed) across all non-duplicate same-fingerprint attestations, and ConflictsWithBundleID/ConflictsWithRating cite the highest-severity conflicting prior (see note for full field spec and test matrix). No reviewer's own Rating is ever overwritten. Auto-dispatch of a tie-break reviewer is explicitly out of scope for this story. Closes narrow-gaps-addendum G3.1 and G3.3 (not G3.2's dispatch option)."}]
["amend","LNGHZN-S7",1784687115,"5207ee28-cdd8-48e6-98dc-7da179d4a40d",{"scope":["internal/config/config.go","internal/config/config_test.go","internal/config/strict.go","internal/config/strict_test.go","cmd/armature/render_context.go","cmd/armature/claim.go","cmd/armature/claim_test.go","internal/doctor/config_check.go","internal/doctor/config_check_test.go","docs/use-cases.md","docs/configuration.md"],"acceptance":["TestDefaultTTLGovernsClaim_REQ_LNGHZN_S7_T1 passes","TestTokenBudgetHonoredByRenderContext_REQ_LNGHZN_S7_T1 passes","TestStrictDecodeRejectsUnknownField_REQ_LNGHZN_S7_T2 passes","TestDoctorConfigCheckD9_REQ_LNGHZN_S7_T2 passes","grep of use-cases.md and configuration.md finds no inert-knob caveat or false-claim language for config fields","arm doctor and arm validate exit 0 after changes","make check green"],"definition_of_done":"Every field in .armature/config.json either governs the behavior its name implies or is deleted: default_ttl becomes the single source of arm claim's --ttl flag default (it already governs staleness elsewhere in hook.go/workers.go); token_budget becomes the single source of arm render-context's --budget flag default; low_stakes_push_threshold is confirmed already wired (coalescing push counter) and its docs are corrected from hedge language to a plain description. Unknown fields are rejected at decode with an error naming the offending key; arm doctor gains check D9 verifying config health; docs/use-cases.md and docs/configuration.md drop inert-knob caveats and false claims."}]
["amend","LNGHZN-S7-T1",1784687125,"5207ee28-cdd8-48e6-98dc-7da179d4a40d",{"scope":["internal/config/config.go","internal/config/config_test.go","cmd/armature/render_context.go","cmd/armature/claim.go","cmd/armature/claim_test.go"],"acceptance":["TestDefaultTTLGovernsClaim_REQ_LNGHZN_S7_T1 passes","TestTokenBudgetHonoredByRenderContext_REQ_LNGHZN_S7_T1 passes","make check green"],"definition_of_done":"default_ttl becomes the single source of arm claim's --ttl flag default (an explicit --ttl flag still overrides it); default_ttl already governs staleness elsewhere (cmd/armature/hook.go:93, cmd/armature/workers.go:32) — this task makes claim's flag default consistent with that same field, not wiring it from scratch. token_budget becomes the single source of arm render-context's --budget flag default (an explicit --budget flag still overrides it). low_stakes_push_threshold is out of scope for this task: it is already wired (cmd/armature/helpers.go:243-259, a coalescing push counter) and needs no code change."}]
["note","LNGHZN-S7-T1",1784687137,"5207ee28-cdd8-48e6-98dc-7da179d4a40d",{"msg":"Grilling session (LNGHZN-S7): low_stakes_push_threshold is already correctly wired at cmd/armature/helpers.go:243-259 (coalescing push counter) — removed from this task, it is not a dead knob. default_ttl is already wired in cmd/armature/hook.go:93 and cmd/armature/workers.go:32 for staleness detection; this task only needs cmd/armature/claim.go's --ttl flag default (currently hardcoded to 60) to read the same config field.","note_id":"note-1784687137858958484"}]
["amend","LNGHZN-S7-T2",1784687137,"5207ee28-cdd8-48e6-98dc-7da179d4a40d",{"acceptance":["TestStrictDecodeRejectsUnknownField_REQ_LNGHZN_S7_T2 passes","TestDoctorConfigCheckD9_REQ_LNGHZN_S7_T2 passes","make check green"],"definition_of_done":"Config decoding rejects unknown fields with an error naming the offending key. arm doctor gains check D9 (D8 is already claimed by TOPTIER-S12-T2's ops-branch remote-tracking check) that validates config.json decodes strictly and every present field is within its valid range, so the config file can never silently lie again."}]
["note","LNGHZN-S7-T2",1784687138,"5207ee28-cdd8-48e6-98dc-7da179d4a40d",{"msg":"Grilling session (LNGHZN-S7): TOPTIER-S12-T2 (also open) already hardcodes doctor check ID D8 for an unrelated ops-branch remote-tracking check, in its own DoD and test name. Pinned this task's new check to D9 to avoid a collision if both land. If TOPTIER-S12-T2 is renumbered or dropped, revisit.","note_id":"note-1784687138105006121"}]
["amend","LNGHZN-S7-T3",1784687148,"5207ee28-cdd8-48e6-98dc-7da179d4a40d",{"scope":["docs/use-cases.md","docs/configuration.md"],"acceptance":["grep of use-cases.md and configuration.md finds no inert-knob caveat or false-claim language for config fields","make check green (doc validation passes)"],"definition_of_done":"use-cases.md §P4 no longer documents default_ttl or token_budget as inert or caveated; each field's description matches its wired behavior. The low_stakes_push_threshold line is reworded from a hedge (\"not an auto-push trigger\") to a positive description of its coalescing design — it is not deleted, since the behavior is real and correct. docs/configuration.md is corrected to match: it currently falsely states arm render-context already respects token_budget, and describes default_ttl's staleness role without mentioning that arm claim's separate --ttl default is fixed in T1. Deleted fields are removed from all examples in both files."}]
["note","LNGHZN-S7-T3",1784687148,"5207ee28-cdd8-48e6-98dc-7da179d4a40d",{"msg":"Grilling session (LNGHZN-S7): docs/configuration.md (not originally in scope) falsely states that arm render-context already respects token_budget (lines 100-105), and describes default_ttl's staleness role (lines 112-115) without mentioning that arm claim's --ttl default is separately broken and fixed in T1. Added to scope alongside use-cases.md. Also: the low_stakes_push_threshold caveat line should be reworded, not deleted — investigation (cmd/armature/helpers.go:243-259) confirmed the coalescing behavior it describes is real and correct.","note_id":"note-1784687148240185848"}]
["amend","LNGHZN-S8",1784687171,"5207ee28-cdd8-48e6-98dc-7da179d4a40d",{"acceptance":["All child tasks merged","arm validate passes with no errors","arm review record behavior is regression-tested unchanged after the orchestrator extraction","Reviewer skill instructs running arm review validate before arm review record"],"definition_of_done":"arm review validate exposes the complete set of validations that arm review record performs (schema, criterion-ID format, citation line-bounds against diff hunks, coverage checks, and activity-citation/digest checks) via a single shared orchestrating function in internal/review that both record.go and the new command call — no independently re-implemented or re-listed checks. The command is read-only (no assessment-file mutation), accepts the same --bundle/assessment input shape as arm review record, and emits structured JSON (agent format: check-id, location, message, suggested remediation) plus human-readable output. It is advisory only: arm review record remains the sole enforcement gate. The reviewer skill is updated to instruct reviewers to run arm review validate and self-correct before calling arm review record. arm review record's existing accept/reject behavior and output are regression-tested as unchanged by the refactor."}]
