["transition","LNGHZN-S4",1785024153,"5207ee28-cdd8-48e6-98dc-7da179d4a40d",{"to":"done","outcome":"Delivered a transition-time delivery gate: internal/deliverygate package with three checks (clean tree, scope containment, commit reference), wired into 'arm transition --to done' via a --skip-delivery-gate override flag (audited in the transition op payload), and documented in the worker skill and use-cases.md. Holistic code review found and fixed two real bugs before merge: scope entries carrying a '(new)' annotation were never stripped before exact-path matching (broke ScopeContainmentCheck on nearly any task with new files in scope), and the base-commit resolution used a hand-rolled ancestor walk preferring a stale local main over origin/main (caused false out-of-scope diffs on sequential tasks). Both fixed with a real git-merge-base-backed implementation and verified by an independent re-review. Full test suite, lint, and 100% mutation efficacy green. Self-transitioning with --skip-delivery-gate: story-level transitions have no declared scope of their own, and the sandbox environment's bind-mounted device files (.bashrc, .claude/agents, etc.) show as dirty-tree noise unrelated to any commit.","skipped_delivery_gate":true}]
