["create","LNGHZN-S9",1785682286,"5207ee28-cdd8-48e6-98dc-7da179d4a40d",{"title":"arm claim --from: Armature-owned branch creation for sub-task worktrees","parent":"LNGHZN","type":"story","acceptance":["LNGHZN-S9-T1 and LNGHZN-S9-T2 delivered and merged","arm validate passes with no errors","PR #88 review thread claim.go:666 closed referencing this story"],"definition_of_done":"arm claim supports a --from \u003cparent-worktree-path\u003e flag that creates a new task branch cut live from the parent worktree's current branch, persisting the same parent-branch config and base-commit metadata the fresh-worktree claim path already writes, so tier-1 dynamic base-commit resolution works for sub-tasks cut from an already-open story worktree without adopting an externally pre-created branch after the fact.","priority":"medium","confidence":"draft"}]
["create","LNGHZN-S9-T1",1785682286,"5207ee28-cdd8-48e6-98dc-7da179d4a40d",{"title":"Implement arm claim --from \u003cparent-worktree-path\u003e","parent":"LNGHZN-S9","type":"task","scope":["cmd/armature/claim.go","cmd/armature/claim_test.go"],"acceptance":["TestClaimFromFlagCreatesBranchFromParentWorktree_REQ_LNGHZN_S9_T1 passes: given a story worktree on branch feat/STORY with a sibling commit, arm claim TASK --worktree \u003cnew\u003e --from \u003cstory-worktree-path\u003e creates task/TASK branched from feat/STORY's current tip, persists branch.task/TASK.armature-parent=feat/STORY, and persists armature-base-commit equal to feat/STORY's HEAD at that moment","TestClaimFromFlagRejectsExistingWorktreePath_REQ_LNGHZN_S9_T1 passes: arm claim --worktree \u003cpath-that-already-exists\u003e --from \u003cparent\u003e returns a usage error and does not touch the existing worktree's bindings","TestClaimFromFlagRejectsUnresolvableFrom_REQ_LNGHZN_S9_T1 passes: arm claim --from \u003cpath-not-a-worktree\u003e returns a clear error and does not create a branch or worktree","TestClaimWithoutFromFlagUnchanged_REQ_LNGHZN_S9_T1 passes: existing fresh-worktree and existing-worktree claim behavior is unaffected when --from is omitted","make check green"],"definition_of_done":"arm claim \u003cissueID\u003e --worktree \u003cnew-path\u003e --from \u003cparent-worktree-path\u003e is accepted only when \u003cnew-path\u003e does not yet exist. --from is resolved as an existing worktree; its CurrentBranch() is used both as the ref createWorktreeAndBranch branches the new task branch from, and as the value persisted via writeParentBranchConfigIfAbsent as the parent-branch git config. No merge-base/fork-point computation is performed for this path, since the branch is cut live from --from's current tip at creation time. When --from is omitted, existing claim behavior (fresh-worktree and existing-worktree paths) is unchanged. When --from is supplied and \u003cnew-path\u003e already exists, claim returns a usage error.","priority":"medium","confidence":"draft"}]
["create","LNGHZN-S9-T2",1785682286,"5207ee28-cdd8-48e6-98dc-7da179d4a40d",{"title":"Document arm claim --from and narrow the existing-worktree limitation note","parent":"LNGHZN-S9","type":"task","scope":["docs/use-cases.md","docs/commands.md","internal/skillsembed/skills/armature-worker/SKILL.md"],"acceptance":["make validate-skills passes","docs/commands.md shows a worked --from example","docs/use-cases.md limitation note updated to scope the remaining gap to manually-created worktrees only"],"definition_of_done":"docs/commands.md documents the new --from flag with an example. docs/use-cases.md's 'Known limitation — worktrees claimed from a pre-existing checkout' section is updated to note that Armature-driven sub-task creation should use --from instead of relying on the existing-worktree adoption path, and that the documented limitation now applies only to worktrees a human creates by hand outside Armature. The armature-worker skill's claim guidance mentions --from for the sub-task-in-story-worktree scenario.","priority":"low","confidence":"draft"}]
