["amend","LNGHZN-S9-T1",1785682313,"5207ee28-cdd8-48e6-98dc-7da179d4a40d",{"definition_of_done":"arm claim \u003cissueID\u003e --worktree \u003cnew-path\u003e --from \u003cparent-worktree-path\u003e is accepted only when \u003cnew-path\u003e does not exist. --from resolves as an existing worktree; its CurrentBranch() is used both as the ref to branch the new task branch from and as the persisted parent-branch git config. No merge-base computation is needed since the branch is cut live from --from's current tip."}]
["amend","LNGHZN-S9-T2",1785682313,"5207ee28-cdd8-48e6-98dc-7da179d4a40d",{"definition_of_done":"docs/commands.md documents the --from flag with an example. docs/use-cases.md's known-limitation note is updated: Armature-driven sub-task creation should use --from; the documented gap now applies only to worktrees a human creates by hand outside Armature. armature-worker skill mentions --from for the sub-task-in-story-worktree case."}]
["amend","NXTTN-S3-T1",1785682729,"5207ee28-cdd8-48e6-98dc-7da179d4a40d",{"definition_of_done":"A context-report command/target enumerates static agent-facing artifacts (embedded skills, CONTEXT.md, docs/commands.md, concepts, use-cases) and reports byte and estimated token weight (bytes/4 heuristic, matching token_budget convention) per artifact, in human and JSON output, documenting the estimation method in the output itself. Dynamic artifacts (render-context output, --format agent payloads) are out of scope, noted as a known limitation."}]
["amend","LNGHZN-S7-T3",1785682729,"5207ee28-cdd8-48e6-98dc-7da179d4a40d",{"definition_of_done":"use-cases.md §P4 no longer documents default_ttl or token_budget as inert/caveated; each field's description matches its wired behavior. low_stakes_push_threshold's line is reworded from a hedge to a positive description of its coalescing design (not deleted; behavior is real). docs/configuration.md is corrected to match (see Notes for specifics). Deleted fields are removed from all examples in both files."}]
["amend","TOPTIER-S13",1785682729,"5207ee28-cdd8-48e6-98dc-7da179d4a40d",{"definition_of_done":"arm review record defines and enforces reviewer-disagreement behavior for repeated assessments of the same delivery fingerprint: same DeliveryFingerprint + differing overall Rating sets IsDisagreement, EffectiveRating is the severity-max across all non-duplicate same-fingerprint attestations, and ConflictsWithBundleID/ConflictsWithRating cite the highest-severity conflicting prior (full field spec and test matrix in Notes). No reviewer's own Rating is ever overwritten. Auto-dispatch of a tie-break reviewer is out of scope. Closes narrow-gaps-addendum G3.1 and G3.3 only."}]
["amend","NXTTN-S3",1785682736,"5207ee28-cdd8-48e6-98dc-7da179d4a40d",{"definition_of_done":"Tokens are a governed budget the way coverage already is: make context-report prices every static agent-facing artifact (skills, glossary, key docs) using a bytes/4 token estimate, per-artifact budgets grouped by class with a shrink-only ratchet are enforced by a check wired into make check, and the coordinator skill is trimmed as the first application. Dynamic artifacts (render-context output, --format agent payloads) are explicitly out of scope for this story."}]
["amend","LNGHZN-S7-T1",1785682736,"5207ee28-cdd8-48e6-98dc-7da179d4a40d",{"definition_of_done":"default_ttl becomes the single source of arm claim's --ttl flag default (explicit --ttl still overrides); it already governs staleness elsewhere (hook.go:93, workers.go:32) — this only makes claim's default consistent. token_budget becomes the single source of render-context's --budget flag default (explicit --budget still overrides). low_stakes_push_threshold is out of scope: already wired (helpers.go:243-259), needs no code change."}]
["amend","LNGHZN-S7",1785682737,"5207ee28-cdd8-48e6-98dc-7da179d4a40d",{"definition_of_done":"Every field in .armature/config.json either governs the behavior its name implies or is deleted: default_ttl becomes the single source of claim's --ttl default (already governs staleness in hook.go/workers.go); token_budget becomes the single source of render-context's --budget default; low_stakes_push_threshold is confirmed already wired and its docs corrected from hedge language. Unknown fields are rejected at decode by key; arm doctor gains D9 config-health check; docs drop inert-knob caveats."}]
["amend","LNGHZN-S8",1785682741,"5207ee28-cdd8-48e6-98dc-7da179d4a40d",{"definition_of_done":"arm review validate exposes the same validations arm review record performs (schema, criterion-ID format, citation line-bounds, coverage, activity-citation/digest checks) via a single shared orchestrating function in internal/review used by both — no re-implemented checks. Read-only, same --bundle/assessment input as record, structured JSON + human output. Advisory only: record remains sole enforcement gate. Reviewer skill updated to run validate first."}]
["amend","TOPTIER-S13",1785682754,"5207ee28-cdd8-48e6-98dc-7da179d4a40d",{"definition_of_done":"arm review record enforces reviewer-disagreement behavior for repeat assessments of the same delivery fingerprint: same DeliveryFingerprint + differing overall Rating sets IsDisagreement; EffectiveRating is the severity-max across non-duplicate same-fingerprint attestations; ConflictsWithBundleID/Rating cite the highest-severity conflict (spec in Notes). Ratings are never overwritten. Tie-break auto-dispatch is out of scope. Closes G3.1/G3.3 only."}]
["amend","LNGHZN-S7",1785682755,"5207ee28-cdd8-48e6-98dc-7da179d4a40d",{"definition_of_done":"Every .armature/config.json field either governs the behavior its name implies or is deleted: default_ttl becomes claim's --ttl default (already governs staleness in hook.go/workers.go); token_budget becomes render-context's --budget default; low_stakes_push_threshold confirmed already wired, docs corrected. Unknown fields rejected at decode by key; doctor gains D9 config-health check; docs drop inert-knob caveats."}]
