["transition","LNGHZN-S5",1786201951,"5207ee28-cdd8-48e6-98dc-7da179d4a40d",{"to":"done","outcome":"Managed worktree lifecycle delivered: T4 boolean --worktree auto-provisions at .worktrees/\u003cid\u003e (detached-then-branch race fix); T1 records worktree_path on claim op (materialized, legacy-replay safe); T2 'arm worktree list|gc' reconciles bound/orphan/ghost by live claim with symlink-safe paths, terminal-status ghost exclusion, deterministic sorted output, and prefix-guarded isManaged; T5 propagates boolean --worktree across docs/skills/harness/golden + ADR; T3 wires a main-tree go.work isolation mitigation at provision time + lifecycle docs. Holistic opus review remediation applied (dead-code wiring, reconcile correctness bugs, ADR renumber 0013, worktree depguard boundary). make check fully green: coverage 85.7%, mutation efficacy 100%."}]
["create","LNGHZN-S5-T6",1786285110,"5207ee28-cdd8-48e6-98dc-7da179d4a40d",{"title":"Unify worktree identity: separate existence from selection","parent":"LNGHZN-S5","type":"task","scope":["internal/worktree/inventory.go,internal/worktree/inventory_test.go,internal/worktree/reconcile.go,internal/worktree/reconcile_test.go,cmd/armature/claim.go,cmd/armature/claim_test.go,cmd/armature/merged.go,cmd/armature/merged_test.go,internal/doctor/fix.go,internal/doctor/fix_test.go,CONTEXT.md"],"acceptance":["worktree.AnyBound reports existence and is documented as never usable to choose a target","worktree.SelectByIssue returns a tri-state Resolution (Bound/NotFound/Ambiguous) and is documented as the only result that may reach a destructive git operation","claim adoption selects on binding, not branch: a marker-bound worktree on the issue branch is adopted; marker-bound but detached or on another branch fails closed naming the path and HEAD state, and provisions nothing","extractIssueIDFromWorktreePath is deleted; a marker-less worktree reconciles to Unrecognized, never BOUND","merged separates read-only gate lookup from destructive resolution by type, so the branch fallback cannot reach git worktree remove --force","doctor PlanFixes uses the existence function and its behaviour is unchanged: a live claim with two marker-bound worktrees is not released","CONTEXT.md defines Issue Binding as authoritative and adds Managed Worktree, Canonical Worktree Path, Adoption, and the reconciliation classes","make check green"],"definition_of_done":"Worktree identity has one authority and two distinct questions. The armature-issue-id binding is the sole identity authority; branch name and directory basename are never used to establish identity. Existence ('is any worktree bound to this issue?') and selection ('which single worktree do I act on?') are separate named functions: existence may be over-inclusive, selection fails closed on ambiguity, and only a selection result may reach a destructive git operation. Every call site (claim adoption, merged gate and removal, worktree gc, doctor fix) delegates to those two functions rather than hand-rolling a precedence. The vocabulary is recorded in CONTEXT.md so call site N+1 cannot invent a fourth authority. Closes the two open review threads on PR #89 (claim.go branch-filtered adoption; reconcile.go basename fallback).","context_files":["CONTEXT.md","CONSTITUTION.md","docs/agents/workflow.md"],"priority":"high","confidence":"draft"}]
["create","LNGHZN-S5-T7",1786285110,"5207ee28-cdd8-48e6-98dc-7da179d4a40d",{"title":"Rename worktree binding identifiers to the glossary term","parent":"LNGHZN-S5","type":"task","scope":["internal/worktree/,internal/doctor/,internal/harnesshook/,cmd/armature/"],"acceptance":["worktree.Meta.IssueID is renamed to Binding and all call sites compile against the new name","no occurrence of 'marker' remains as a synonym for the issue binding in comments under internal/ or cmd/","the diff is a pure rename: no control-flow or test-assertion changes","make check green"],"definition_of_done":"Code identifiers use the CONTEXT.md term for worktree identity. worktree.Meta.IssueID becomes Binding, and 'marker' disappears from comments in favour of 'binding'. One glossary term, one code name, across internal/worktree, internal/doctor, internal/harnesshook and cmd/armature. Pure rename: no behaviour change, no test-expectation change beyond the identifier.","context_files":["CONTEXT.md"],"priority":"medium","confidence":"draft"}]
