["transition","LNGHZN-S5-T6",1786287556,"5207ee28-cdd8-48e6-98dc-7da179d4a40d",{"to":"done","outcome":"Split worktree identity into two questions with distinct APIs. worktree.SelectByIssue returns a tri-state Resolution (Bound/NotFound/Ambiguous) and is documented as the only result that may reach a destructive git operation; worktree.AnyBound answers existence, is over-inclusive by design, and returns no entry so it cannot choose a target. The armature-issue-id binding is the sole identity authority: branch name and directory basename establish nothing. claim.go adoption selects by binding, so a worktree bound to the issue but detached or on a scratch branch is found rather than duplicated, and fails closed instead of being relocated mid-git-operation (closes PR #89 P1 thread on claim.go:332). reconcile.go's basename fallback is deleted, so a marker-less worktree is Unrecognized instead of falsely BOUND (closes PR #89 P2 thread on reconcile.go:103). merged.go separates findGateTarget (returns a git dir to read, keeps the unbound-on-branch widening that closes the violation-gate enforcement gap) from resolveBoundWorktree (returns a worktree to act on, binding only), so branch name is structurally unable to reach --force. doctor/fix.go delegates to AnyBound with behaviour unchanged; a new test pins that an ambiguous binding never releases a live claim. 15 reconcile tests were updated to set IssueID -- they had been exercising the deleted fallback rather than the production path, which is why the defect survived five review rounds -- and the worktree_test.go fixture now builds a genuine orphan plus a distinct unrecognized case. CONTEXT.md records the vocabulary: Issue Binding gains an authority clause, plus Managed Worktree, Canonical Worktree Path, Adoption, and the five reconciliation classes. make check green: coverage 85.7% (worktree 87.1%), mutation efficacy 100% (internal killed=1829 lived=0, cmd killed=1096 lived=0), golangci-lint 0 issues, census drift clean."}]
["create","LNGHZN-S5-T9",1786288773,"5207ee28-cdd8-48e6-98dc-7da179d4a40d",{"title":"Clear branch-point provenance from the recorded claimed branch","parent":"LNGHZN-S5","type":"task","scope":["cmd/armature/merged.go,cmd/armature/merged_test.go"],"acceptance":["teardown reads the recorded claimed branch before the marker is deleted","a worktree removed while on a scratch branch leaves no armature.parent-branch config for its task branch","reusing the task branch name afterwards resolves a correct delivery range","make check green"],"definition_of_done":"Worktree teardown clears branch-point provenance keyed on the branch the issue was actually claimed under, not the branch the worktree happens to be on at removal time. The immutable armature-claimed-branch marker is the authority, with the derived issue branch as a legacy fallback only. A worktree torn down while parked on a scratch branch leaves no stale armature.parent-branch entry behind.","context_files":["CONTEXT.md"],"priority":"medium","confidence":"draft"}]
["create","LNGHZN-S5-T10",1786288773,"5207ee28-cdd8-48e6-98dc-7da179d4a40d",{"title":"Report ambiguous candidates from worktree gc --dry-run","parent":"LNGHZN-S5","type":"task","scope":["cmd/armature/worktree.go,cmd/armature/worktree_test.go"],"acceptance":["gc --dry-run lists ambiguous issue IDs in both human and JSON output","gc --dry-run exits non-zero when the ambiguous set is non-empty","gc --dry-run still exits zero when there is simply nothing to remove","make check green"],"definition_of_done":"arm worktree gc --dry-run surfaces ambiguous binding candidates exactly as a real gc run does: they appear in its output and it exits non-zero. A dry run and a real run agree about whether the repository is in an anomalous state, so agent automation cannot read a preview as all-clear.","context_files":["CONTEXT.md"],"priority":"medium","confidence":"draft"}]
