["note","LNGHZN-S5-T6",1786288849,"5207ee28-cdd8-48e6-98dc-7da179d4a40d",{"msg":"Reopened for round-6 P1 remediation: the adoption loop collected only the first binding match, so a second worktree sharing the issue binding was never observed and stayed behind as a force-removal candidate. This is the same ambiguity policy worktree.SelectByIssue enforces; adoption was the one call site still hand-rolling its own loop rather than collecting the full bound set.","note_id":"note-1786288849896504124"}]
["transition","LNGHZN-S5-T6",1786289395,"5207ee28-cdd8-48e6-98dc-7da179d4a40d",{"to":"done","outcome":"Split worktree identity into two questions with distinct APIs. worktree.SelectByIssue returns a tri-state Resolution (Bound/NotFound/Ambiguous) and is the only result that may reach a destructive git operation; worktree.AnyBound answers existence, is over-inclusive by design, and returns no entry so it cannot choose a target. The armature-issue-id binding is the sole identity authority: branch name and directory basename establish nothing. claim.go adoption collects the FULL bound set before moving anything, fails closed on more than one match naming every candidate (round-6 P1), and fails closed when the single bound worktree is detached or on a scratch branch rather than duplicating it (round-5 P1, PR #89 claim.go:332). reconcile.go's basename fallback is deleted, so a marker-less worktree is Unrecognized instead of falsely BOUND (round-5 P2, PR #89 reconcile.go:103). merged.go separates findGateTarget (returns a git dir to read, keeps the unbound-on-branch widening that closes the violation-gate enforcement gap) from resolveBoundWorktree (returns a worktree to act on, binding only), so branch name is structurally unable to reach --force. doctor/fix.go delegates to AnyBound with behaviour unchanged; a test pins that an ambiguous binding never releases a live claim. 15 reconcile tests were updated to set IssueID -- they had been exercising the deleted fallback rather than the production path, which is why the defect survived five review rounds -- and the worktree_test.go fixture now builds a genuine orphan plus a distinct unrecognized case. CONTEXT.md records the vocabulary: Issue Binding gains an authority clause, plus Managed Worktree, Canonical Worktree Path, Adoption, and the five reconciliation classes. Two non-blocking round-6 findings were triaged out to LNGHZN-S5-T9 (branch-point provenance cleared from the current branch rather than the recorded claimed branch) and LNGHZN-S5-T10 (gc --dry-run does not report ambiguous candidates). make check green: coverage 85.8%, mutation efficacy 100% (internal killed=1829 lived=0, cmd killed=1095 lived=0), golangci-lint 0 issues, census drift clean."}]
