["create","LNGHZN-S10-T6",1786751117,"5207ee28-cdd8-48e6-98dc-7da179d4a40d",{"title":"Scope overlap must match on files/globs, not containing directory","parent":"LNGHZN-S10","type":"task","scope":["internal/claim/overlap.go,internal/claim/overlap_test.go"],"definition_of_done":"globOverlaps in internal/claim/overlap.go no longer reports an overlap for two distinct files that merely share a containing directory or an ancestor directory: the extractDir/hasPrefix fallback is removed from the blocking path, and overlap is decided by actual path or glob match only. Directory ownership must still be expressible and still conflict correctly when declared as an explicit glob (docs/agents/**). Regression tests cover: docs/agents/quality-gates.md vs docs/use-cases.md =\u003e NO overlap; README.md vs README.md =\u003e overlap; docs/agents/** vs docs/agents/quality-gates.md =\u003e overlap; internal/claim/overlap.go vs internal/claim/overlap_test.go =\u003e NO overlap. arm claim LNGHZN-S10-T2 succeeds without --force after the fix, and the arm validate scope-overlap warning count drops substantially.","context_files":["docs/dogfood/findings/raw/2026-08-14T2352Z-5207ee28-tooling-scope-overlap-matches-on-directory-not-file.md"],"priority":"high","confidence":"draft"}]
