["note","LNGHZN-S10-T6",1786752474,"5207ee28-cdd8-48e6-98dc-7da179d4a40d",{"msg":"Coordinator verification of acceptance criterion 3 (2026-08-14): built the fix to a temp binary (not make install, to avoid swapping the global arm out from under a concurrent session) and ran 'arm claim LNGHZN-S10-T2 --ttl 240 --worktree' — succeeded without --force. Criterion 3 SATISFIED; supersedes the reviewer's indeterminate on acceptance[2], which was delegated to the coordinator by design. Separately discovered that arm validate's scope-overlap warning count did NOT move (196 before and after) because internal/validate/validate.go:372-385 carries a duplicate copy of the same buggy globOverlaps with a globOverlapDir fallback. That is outside T6's contract and is filed as LNGHZN-S10-T7, which now also blocks T4.","note_id":"note-1786752474388622160"}]
