["create","LNGHZN-S10-T8",1786752866,"5207ee28-cdd8-48e6-98dc-7da179d4a40d",{"title":"arm claim must not treat an in-progress story as a competing claimant","parent":"LNGHZN-S10","type":"task","scope":["cmd/armature/claim.go"],"definition_of_done":"The claim-time scope-collision loop in cmd/armature/claim.go considers only issues a worker can hold: type task in claimed or in-progress state, matching the non-task filter internal/validate already applies in its W1 check. An in-progress story no longer blocks claims of overlapping tasks in other stories. The overlap error names the conflicting issue's type and holder so a false block is diagnosable without reading the source.","priority":"high","confidence":"draft"}]
["create","LNGHZN-S10-T9",1786752894,"5207ee28-cdd8-48e6-98dc-7da179d4a40d",{"title":"Resolve P1 review findings from PR #102: glob-vs-glob overlap, and normative rules that precede their mechanism","parent":"LNGHZN-S10","type":"task","scope":["internal/claim/overlap.go"],"definition_of_done":"P1-1: scope overlap detects a non-empty intersection between two glob patterns, not only glob-to-literal containment, so src/auth/*.go and src/auth/login.* are reported as overlapping. P1-2: the reviewer skill's evidence-only acceptance rule no longer forces not_satisfied while no evidence mechanism exists, via an explicit not-yet-enforceable state distinct from indeterminate. P1-3: the worker skill no longer mandates make check-fast before that target exists, using the same not-yet-enforceable treatment.","priority":"high","confidence":"draft"}]
["amend","LNGHZN-S10-T9",1786752894,"5207ee28-cdd8-48e6-98dc-7da179d4a40d",{"scope":["internal/claim/overlap.go","internal/claim/overlap_test.go","internal/scopematch/scopematch.go","internal/scopematch/scopematch_test.go","internal/skillsembed/skills/armature-reviewer/SKILL.md","internal/skillsembed/skills/armature-worker/SKILL.md"],"acceptance":["TestOverlapDetectsGlobToGlobIntersection_REQ_LNGHZN_S10_T9: src/auth/*.go vs src/auth/login.* reports overlap, in both directions","Existing no-overlap cases still hold: docs/agents/quality-gates.md vs docs/use-cases.md reports NO overlap, and identical paths and glob-to-file cases still report overlap","The armature-reviewer skill defines a not-yet-enforceable state, distinct from indeterminate, and the gate-evidence acceptance rule uses it so a missing evidence op cannot force a red verdict while arm gate run does not exist","The armature-worker skill no longer mandates make check-fast unconditionally, and states the condition under which it becomes mandatory","make check is green"]}]
