["note","LNGHZN-S10-T8",1786752946,"5207ee28-cdd8-48e6-98dc-7da179d4a40d",{"msg":"Claim required --force (2026-08-15, coordinator 5207ee28). Reviewed before overriding: the only conflicting entry was story LNGHZN-S7 itself, whose aggregate scope includes cmd/armature/claim.go. No S7 task held a claim (T1 merged, T2 and T3 open), so no worker could be writing that file. This is precisely the false block T8 exists to fix, so the fix is unreachable without one override. arm recorded overlap notes on both issues as the audit trail.","note_id":"note-1786752946164084767"}]
["heartbeat","LNGHZN-S10-T8",1786753074,"5207ee28-cdd8-48e6-98dc-7da179d4a40d",{"source":"hook"}]
["amend","LNGHZN-S10-T9",1786753311,"5207ee28-cdd8-48e6-98dc-7da179d4a40d",{"scope":["internal/skillsembed/skills/armature-reviewer/SKILL.md","internal/skillsembed/skills/armature-worker/SKILL.md"],"acceptance":["The armature-reviewer skill defines a not-yet-enforceable state, distinct from indeterminate, and its gate-evidence acceptance rule uses it so a missing evidence op cannot force a red verdict while arm gate run does not exist (LNGHZN-S10-T3)","The armature-worker skill no longer mandates make check-fast unconditionally and names LNGHZN-S10-T2 as the task that makes it enforceable","Each not-yet-enforceable rule names the task that lifts it, so the state cannot become a permanent waiver","make validate-skills is green"],"definition_of_done":"The reviewer and worker skills gain an explicit not-yet-enforceable state, distinct from indeterminate, so a normative rule whose mechanism has not shipped cannot force a red verdict or mandate a missing make target. The reviewer's gate-evidence acceptance rule and the worker's make check-fast mandate both use it, each naming the task that makes it enforceable."}]
["note","LNGHZN-S10-T9",1786753311,"5207ee28-cdd8-48e6-98dc-7da179d4a40d",{"msg":"Scope narrowed 2026-08-15 by HITL decision (Brian Scully): P1-1 from PR #102 (glob-vs-glob intersection in internal/claim/overlap.go) is a defect in LNGHZN-S10-T6's own diff and is being remediated in place on task/LNGHZN-S10-T6 as review cycle 1, before #102 merges, so main never carries the under-blocking window. T9 now covers only P1-2 and P1-3, which are defects in LNGHZN-S10-T1's delivery and need the not-yet-enforceable design.","note_id":"note-1786753311872905727"}]
