["note","LNGHZN-S10-T7",1786754978,"5207ee28-cdd8-48e6-98dc-7da179d4a40d",{"msg":"COORDINATOR FLAG (2026-08-15, pre-handoff): the T7 worktree has an uncommitted change to .golangci.yml, which is OUTSIDE T7's declared scope (internal/validate/validate.go, internal/validate/validate_test.go, internal/scopematch/scopematch.go, internal/scopematch/scopematch_test.go, internal/claim/overlap.go). The change adds internal/scopematch to a depguard allowed-imports list, because internal/validate now imports internal/scopematch as a result of the de-duplication. Assessment: legitimate and necessary - it declares a new architectural dependency edge, it is not lint being relaxed to mask a failure. But it IS an architecture boundary rule change and needs explicit human sign-off rather than silent inclusion. If committed as-is the harness hook will record a scope violation and arm merged will refuse without --force. Options for the next coordinator: amend T7 scope to include .golangci.yml with this rationale, or split the depguard change into its own reviewed change. Do not simply --force past the violation.","note_id":"note-1786754978663754489"}]
["amend","LNGHZN-S10-T7",1786755021,"5207ee28-cdd8-48e6-98dc-7da179d4a40d",{"scope":["internal/validate/validate.go","internal/validate/validate_test.go","internal/scopematch/scopematch.go","internal/scopematch/scopematch_test.go","internal/claim/overlap.go",".golangci.yml"]}]
["note","LNGHZN-S10-T7",1786755021,"5207ee28-cdd8-48e6-98dc-7da179d4a40d",{"msg":"RESOLVED by HITL (Brian Scully, 2026-08-15): .golangci.yml added to T7 scope. Rationale: the de-duplication makes internal/validate import internal/scopematch, so the depguard allowed-imports list must declare that edge. This is an intended new dependency, not a relaxation of lint to mask a failure; the only change is one added entry. Sign-off recorded here so the boundary change is auditable rather than implicit.","note_id":"note-1786755021236408047"}]
["note","LNGHZN-S10-T6",1786755034,"5207ee28-cdd8-48e6-98dc-7da179d4a40d",{"msg":"HITL DECISION (Brian Scully, 2026-08-15) on the red remediation gate: SHRINK THE FIX, then re-gate. The glob-vs-glob remediation currently sits UNCOMMITTED in .worktrees/LNGHZN-S10-T6 as +102 lines in overlap.go and +81 in overlap_test.go. make check is RED at the mutate step: 'below mutant coverage-threshold, internal: efficacy=100.00% coverage=94.76% killed=1862 lived=0 not_covered=103'. lived=0 means every covered mutant was killed, so existing tests are strong; the failure is 103 mutants in new code no test reaches. Treat the SIZE as the defect: 102 new lines for 'when both sides are globs and a precise answer is not cheap, report overlap' indicates a second heuristic grew where a small predicate was specified. Reduce the implementation until the behaviour fits a few branches, then re-run the gate; the mutation gap is expected to close with the excess rather than needing 103 mutants' worth of new tests. Do NOT add tests to paper over unjustified breadth in the code path that decides whether two agents may write the same file. Constraints unchanged: must not reintroduce the directory-prefix fallback (docs/agents/quality-gates.md vs docs/use-cases.md stays NO overlap) and must stay bounded (src/auth/*.go vs src/billing/*.go stays NO overlap).","note_id":"note-1786755034852541422"}]
