["create","LNGHZN-S10-T11",1786797947,"5207ee28-cdd8-48e6-98dc-7da179d4a40d",{"title":"Extract a TUI seam so interactive code is excludable from coverage and mutation gates","parent":"LNGHZN-S10","type":"task","scope":["cmd/armature/ready.go,cmd/armature/stalereview.go,cmd/armature/dagsum.go,cmd/armature/tui.go,cmd/armature/*_tui.go,.gremlins.yaml,docs/design/gate-efficiency.md"],"definition_of_done":"Interactive terminal-entry code in cmd/armature is extracted into dedicated *_tui.go files containing only the TUI boundary (program construction, model wiring, interactive branch selection). Non-interactive logic stays in the original files and remains covered. .gremlins.yaml excludes the new *_tui.go pattern alongside the existing _windows.go / filelock_other.go precedent. make check passes. Coverage and mutant-coverage for cmd/** are re-measured and the before/after numbers recorded in docs/design/gate-efficiency.md.","context_files":["docs/design/gate-efficiency.md",".gremlins.yaml","Makefile"],"priority":"medium","confidence":"draft"}]
