["decision","LNGHZN-S10-T5",1787510823,"5207ee28-cdd8-48e6-98dc-7da179d4a40d",{"topic":"I7 override: force merged past hook-log violations","choice":"force promotion","rationale":"The 4 violation entries in .git/worktrees/LNGHZN-S10-T5/armature-hook.log are out-of-scope writes to /tmp scratch files (e13doc.py, gatedoc.py, commitmsg.txt, replies.sh; logged as ../../../../../../tmp/claude-1000/...) created during PR #112 review cycles. None is repo work product; delivery is in scope and on main (merge 80dee97c). This is a second I7, distinct from the earlier missing-conformance-review decision: that one does not cover the hook-log gate. Local task/LNGHZN-S10-T5 is a stale leftover (behind main; git cherry all equivalent). Human accepts under I7 and authorizes arm merged --force. Worktree teardown and local branch deletion follow."}]
["decision","LNGHZN-S9-T1",1787510842,"5207ee28-cdd8-48e6-98dc-7da179d4a40d",{"topic":"I7 override: force merged with residual yellow and worktree gone","choice":"force promotion","rationale":"Supersedes the 2026-08-23 I7 that claimed no recorded conformance assessment. Compact attestations exist: 8 assessment-attested ops; latest yellow bundle 868f29ad, 5 satisfied, 1 indeterminate, 0 partial, 0 not_satisfied. T1 never rated green. Residual yellow is indeterminate-only (evidence gap), not a recorded contract failure. Full ConformanceAssessment JSON is gone. Worktree was torn down before promotion, so arm merged cannot read a hook log — irreversible ordering trap, not evidence of a violation. Recreating an empty worktree would launder not-checked into no-violations and is refused. Work is on main: PR #97 merged (4577bf7). Human accepts residual indeterminate yellow plus unverified hook log under I7 and authorizes arm merged --force --pr 97."}]
