["create","LNGHZN-S6-T4",1787512384,"5207ee28-cdd8-48e6-98dc-7da179d4a40d",{"title":"Extract a TUI seam so interactive code is excludable from coverage and mutation gates","parent":"LNGHZN-S6","type":"task","scope":["cmd/armature/ready.go","cmd/armature/stalereview.go","cmd/armature/dagsum.go","cmd/armature/tui.go","cmd/armature/*_tui.go",".gremlins.yaml","docs/design/gate-efficiency.md"],"acceptance":["Interactive TUI construction and model wiring live only in cmd/armature/*_tui.go","Non-interactive logic remains in ready.go, stalereview.go, dagsum.go, and tui.go and stays covered",".gremlins.yaml excludes the *_tui.go pattern","Before/after cmd statement coverage and mutant-coverage are recorded in docs/design/gate-efficiency.md","make check is green"],"definition_of_done":"Extract interactive terminal-entry code from cmd/armature into *_tui.go files that contain only the TUI boundary (program construction, model wiring, interactive branch selection). Non-interactive logic stays in the original files and remains covered. .gremlins.yaml excludes *_tui.go (same precedent as _windows.go). make check passes. Re-measure cmd coverage and mutant-coverage; record before/after in docs/design/gate-efficiency.md.","context_files":["docs/adr/0015-recalibrate-mutation-and-coverage-gates.md","docs/design/gate-efficiency.md",".gremlins.yaml"],"priority":"medium","confidence":"draft"}]
