["create","AOC-S2-T5",1787543046,"5207ee28-cdd8-48e6-98dc-7da179d4a40d",{"title":"Root command behaviour: fail-loud flags, version fast path, content-first home view","parent":"AOC-S2","type":"task","scope":["cmd/armature/main.go","cmd/armature/main_test.go","cmd/armature/version.go"],"acceptance":["TestUnknownFlagRejectedWithValidFlagsListed_REQ_AOC_S2_T5 passes","TestVersionFlagVariantsExitZero_REQ_AOC_S2_T5 passes","TestBareArmShowsReadyQueueInRepo_REQ_AOC_S2_T5 passes","TestBareArmOutsideRepoIsDefinitiveEmptyState_REQ_AOC_S2_T5 passes","make check green"],"definition_of_done":"Unknown or inapplicable flags are rejected by name at exit 2 with the command's valid flags listed inline, rather than being silently dropped. --version, -v and -V each print the bare version and exit 0, matching the existing arm version subcommand. Bare arm in a non-TTY prints the ready queue with a short help[] when the working directory is an Armature repo, and a definitive empty state naming the problem when it is not; a TTY still gets the existing behaviour.","context_files":["docs/design/agent-output-contract.md"],"priority":"high","confidence":"draft"}]
