["create","AOC-S4-T1",1787543046,"5207ee28-cdd8-48e6-98dc-7da179d4a40d",{"title":"Payload-keyed transition idempotency and ADR 0018","parent":"AOC-S4","type":"task","scope":["cmd/armature/transition.go","cmd/armature/transition_test.go","internal/ops/types.go","docs/adr/0018-payload-keyed-op-idempotency.md (new)"],"acceptance":["TestIdenticalPayloadIsNoOpExitZero_REQ_AOC_S4_T1 passes","TestChangedPayloadAppendsAmendment_REQ_AOC_S4_T1 passes","TestNoOpAppendsNothingToOpsLog_REQ_AOC_S4_T1 passes","make check green"],"definition_of_done":"A mutation whose payload is byte-identical to the issue's current recorded state is a no-op: exit 0, nothing appended, said explicitly rather than erroring. A same-status mutation carrying a changed payload is appended as an amendment at exit 0. ADR 0018 records why idempotency is keyed on payload rather than status, and why declining to append an op that cannot change materialized state does not violate I2.","context_files":["docs/design/agent-output-contract.md","CONSTITUTION.md"],"priority":"medium","confidence":"draft"}]
