["amend","AOC-S1-T1",1787745859,"5207ee28-cdd8-48e6-98dc-7da179d4a40d",{"scope":["docs/adr/0017-agent-output-contract.md (new)","docs/design/agent-output-contract.md","docs/design/agent-output-contract-plan.json"],"definition_of_done":"ADR 0017 records the Agent Output Contract: single channel, uniform envelope {count, payload[], help[]}, and the Protocol Output and Artifact Output carve-outs. docs/design/agent-output-contract.md gains a normative section stating the envelope, channel, default list schema, help[] rules, empty-state rules and mode-sensitive classification precisely enough for a lint to be written against it. The implementation plan carries those classifications into the downstream helper, lint and census tasks."}]
["amend","AOC-S3-T3",1787745906,"5207ee28-cdd8-48e6-98dc-7da179d4a40d",{"acceptance":["TestEveryAgentFacingCommandHasConformingFixture_REQ_AOC_S3_T3 passes","TestNewCommandWithoutFixtureFailsLint_REQ_AOC_S3_T3 passes","TestProtocolOutputExemptedByClassificationNotName_REQ_AOC_S3_T3 passes","TestArtifactOutputModesUseForeignShapeAndOtherModesConform_REQ_AOC_S3_T3 passes","make check green"],"definition_of_done":"A lint enumerates every registered cobra command mode. Each agent-facing mode requires a conforming golden; a missing fixture fails make check. Protocol Output and Artifact Output modes are exempt only by explicit classification, never by name. Each Artifact Output mode is checked against its cited foreign shape, while other modes of the same command require envelope fixtures."}]
["amend","AOC-S3-T4",1787745906,"5207ee28-cdd8-48e6-98dc-7da179d4a40d",{"acceptance":["TestCensusCoversOutputShape_REQ_AOC_S3_T4 passes","TestCensusCoversModeSensitiveArtifactOutput_REQ_AOC_S3_T4 passes","make census-drift-check green","make test-census-drift-check green","make check green"],"definition_of_done":"surface-census.md records structured shape and agent-facing / Protocol Output / Artifact Output classification per command mode, including selecting flags and cited shape for Artifact modes. census-drift-check compares rows with code bidirectionally, failing changed classifications or flags without rows and phantom rows without code. The self-test covers the new sections."}]
